519:    * then publishes them to the client. The given worker is called for every received job, works on
520:    * them and eventually completes them.
521:    *
522:    * <pre>
523:    * JobWorker worker = camundaClient
524:    *  .newWorker()
525:    *  .jobType("payment")
526:    *  .handler(paymentHandler)
527:    *  .open();
528:    *
529:    * ...
530:    * worker.close();
531:    * </pre>
532:    *
533:    * Example JobHandler implementation:
534:    *
535:    * <pre>
536:    * public final class PaymentHandler implements JobHandler
537:    * {
538:    *   &#64;Override
539:    *   public void handle(JobClient client, JobEvent jobEvent)
540:    *   {
541:    *     String json = jobEvent.getVariables();
542:    *     // modify variables
543:    *
544:    *     client
545:    *      .newCompleteCommand()
546:    *      .event(jobEvent)
547:    *      .variables(json)
548:    *      .send();
549:    *   }
550:    * };
551:    * </pre>
552:    *
553:    * @return a builder for the worker registration
554:    */
